/**
Naming convention:
    The configuration file is named as snax_<cluster_name>_cluster.hjson
    The cluster name should be matched with the configuration file name, so that this cluster can be integrated into HeMAiA.
    The bender_target of the cluster should be the same as the cluster name.
    If XDMA is added into the cfg, the bender_target of the XDMA inside this cluster should be snax_<cluster_name>_xdma.
    Adding a new "bender_target" also involves adding the corresponding file list in Bender.yml. "snax_<cluster_name>" target includes the cluster shell, streamers, and accelerator and "snax_<cluster_name>_xdma" target includes the XDMA shell and XDMA SystemVerilog.

THIS IS ALSO THE CFG THE HeMAiA MULTI-CLUSTER ChainGather TEST BUILDS FROM.

CHAINGATHER — the cross-cluster collective
------------------------------------------
The `writer_junctions` bank below puts the 2->1 DataPathJunction operators on the xDMA data switch, which is
what enables the CHAINGATHER / GATHERROOT switch modes. A gather hop folds the arriving remote partial with
its OWN local operand and forwards only the result, instead of every node shipping a full partial to one root.

HOW SOFTWARE DRIVES A GATHER  (see snax-xdma-addr.h for the pointers)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The collector issues ONE task; every other participant is passive, exactly like a multicast.

  writerPtr[]   the chain in DATA order, ending at the collector's own destination buffer, e.g.
                [S1, S2, DST_local]. Each entry is that node's REAL partial-buffer address — the routers
                decode only a pointer's cluster tag, so the low bits are free to carry the true offset and
                per-node offsets need no extra cfg field.
  readerPtr     the collector's own partial.
  XDMA_DST_JCT_ENABLE_PTR  bit i = 1 arms junction i. ARMING A JUNCTION IS WHAT MAKES THE TRANSFER A GATHER
                (`collectiveMode := junctionEnabled`) — there is no separate "which collective" CSR.
  XDMA_DST_JCT_CSR_PTR     the junction's own CSR (MonoidJunction: [7:0] nValid, [11:8] n, [21:18] nExp, [25:22] nAdd, [27:26] sigma).

The unroll then emits, per remote hop, a READER-side frame (read your own partial) and a WRITER-side frame
(arm your junction and forward) — two frames, because a frame carries `isWriterSide` and the receiver
demuxes on it, so one frame can configure a reader or a writer but never both. The chain HEAD gets the
reader frame ONLY: nothing arrives at a head, so a writer frame would arm its junction on a stream that
never comes. The TAIL is the collector itself and is configured locally.

ADDRESSING INVARIANT A GATHER DEPENDS ON
----------------------------------------
`max_mem_size_kiB: 4096` makes the cfg routers compare address bits [47:22], i.e. one cluster tag per 4 MB —
and `cluster_base_offset` below is 4 MB. Consecutive clusters therefore land on consecutive tags, which is
what lets a writerPtr entry name both WHICH node a frame is for and WHERE that node's partial lives. Change
one of those two numbers and you must change the other.

`max_multicast: 16` sets the writerPtr[] depth = the maximum chain length (and costs 2 CSRs per entry).

⚠️ HeMAiA INTEGRATION CHECKLIST
-------------------------------
1. `AccompanyCfgBits` is 124, not 123 — the accompany-cfg sideband gained `is_initiator` (task ownership,
   which for a gather sits on the TAIL, not the head). The sideband crosses as ONE PACKED VECTOR, so a
   wrapper built against 123 does not fail loudly: every field shifts by one bit and surfaces as garbage
   dma_length / addresses. Regenerate the wrapper (hw/templates/snax_xdma_wrapper.sv.tpl) and make sure the
   xdma_axi_adapter in use also has `is_initiator`.
2. Regenerate: `make rtl-snax-gen CFG_OVERRIDE=cfg/snax_xdma_cluster.hjson`, then rebuild SW — the junction
   region shifts XDMA_START_PTR onward, and a stale sw/snax/xdma/build/snax-xdma-lib.o carries the OLD CSR
   offsets while `make clean` does not remove it.

STATUS: single-cluster switch modes and the cfg-plane unroll are validated by chiseltest
(XDMADataSwitchTester, ChainUnrollTester). The multi-cluster DATA plane is not yet brought up — that is what
this cfg's junction bank exists to do on HeMAiA.
**/
{
    nr_s1_quadrant: 1,
    s1_quadrant: {
        nr_clusters: 1,
    },

    cluster: {
        name: "snax_xdma_cluster",
        bender_target: ["snitch_cluster", "snax_xdma_cluster", "sparse_interconnect"],
        boot_addr: 4096, // 0x1000
        cluster_base_addr: 268435456, // 0x1000_0000
        cluster_base_offset: 4194304,  // 4MB
        cluster_base_hartid: 0,
        addr_width: 48,
        data_width: 64,
        user_width: 3,
        tcdm: {
            size: 128,
            banks: 32,
            sparse_interconnect: true,
        },
        cluster_periph_size: 64, // kB
        zero_mem_size: 64, // kB
        dma_data_width: 512,
        dma_axi_req_fifo_depth: 16,
        dma_req_fifo_depth: 8,

        // Observable pins parameter
        observable_pin_width: 8,

        // Additional parameters for Hemaia integration
        narrow_trans: 4,
        wide_trans: 32,
        dma_user_width: 1,
        // We don't need Snitch debugging in Hemaia
        enable_debug: false,
        // We don't need Snitch (core-internal) virtual memory support
        vm_support: false,
        // Memory configuration inputs
        sram_cfg_expose: true,
        sram_cfg_fields: {
            ema: 3,
            emaw: 2,
            emas: 1
        },
        snax_custom_tcdm_assign: {
            snax_enable_assign_tcdm_idx: true,
            snax_narrow_assign_start_idx: [0,56],
            snax_narrow_assign_end_idx: [7,71],
            snax_wide_assign_start_idx: [8],
            snax_wide_assign_end_idx: [55],
        },
        // Timing parameters
        timing: {
            lat_comp_fp32: 3,
            lat_comp_fp64: 3,
            lat_comp_fp16: 2,
            lat_comp_fp16_alt: 2,
            lat_comp_fp8: 1,
            lat_comp_fp8_alt: 1,
            lat_noncomp: 1,
            lat_conv: 1,
            lat_sdotp: 2,
            fpu_pipe_config: "BEFORE"
            narrow_xbar_latency: "CUT_ALL_PORTS",
            wide_xbar_latency: "CUT_ALL_PORTS",
            // Isolate the core.
            register_core_req: true,
            register_core_rsp: true,
            register_offload_req: true,
            register_offload_rsp: true,
            register_ext_narrow: true,
            register_ext_wide: true,
        },
        hives: [
            // Hive 0
            {
                icache: {
                    size: 8, // total instruction cache size in kByte
                    sets: 2, // number of ways
                    cacheline: 256 // word size in bits
                },
                cores: [
                    { $ref: "#/snax_streamer_gemmX_core_template" },
                    { $ref: "#/dma_core_template" },
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    dram: {
        // 0x8000_0000
        address: 2147483648,
        // 0x8000_0000
        length: 2147483648
    },
    peripherals: {
        clint: {
            // 0xffff_0000
            address: 4294901760,
            // 0x0000_1000
            length: 4096
        },
    },
    // Templates.
    snax_streamer_gemmX_core_template: {
        isa: "rv32ima",
        xssr: false,
        xfrep: false,
        xdma: false,
        xf16: false,
        xf16alt: false,
        xf8: false,
        xf8alt: false,
        xfdotp: false,
        xfvec: false,
        snax_acc_cfg: [{
            snax_acc_name: "snax_streamer_gemmX",
            bender_target: ["snax_gemmX"],
            snax_tcdm_ports: 56,
            sparse_interconnect_config: [[8, 1], [8, 8], [8, 8], [32, 8]],
            snax_num_rw_csr: 19,
            snax_num_ro_csr: 2,
            snax_gemmx_mesh_row: 8,
            snax_gemmx_tile_size: 8,
            snax_gemmx_mesh_col: 8,
            snax_gemmx_serial_c32_d32_width: 2048,
            snax_gemmx_serial_d8_width: 512,
            with_pipeline: true,
            snax_streamer_cfg: {$ref: "#/snax_streamer_gemmX_streamer_template" }
        }],
        snax_use_custom_ports: false,
        num_int_outstanding_loads: 1,
        num_int_outstanding_mem: 4,
        num_fp_outstanding_loads: 4,
        num_fp_outstanding_mem: 4,
        num_sequencer_instructions: 16,
        num_dtlb_entries: 1,
        num_itlb_entries: 1,
        // Enable division/square root unit
        // Xdiv_sqrt: true,
    },
    // Templates.
    dma_core_template: {
        isa: "rv32ima",
        snax_xdma_cfg:
        {
            bender_target:
            [
                snax_xdma_cluster_xdma
            ]
            cfg_io_width: 32
            // writerPtr[] depth = the maximum ChainGather/multicast chain length (2 CSRs per entry)
            max_multicast: 16
            max_dimension: 5
            max_mem_size_kiB: 4096, // sets the router's cluster-tag LSB to bit 22 -> 4 MB per cluster
            reader_buffer: 12
            writer_buffer: 12
            reader_agu_temporal_dimension: 5
            writer_agu_temporal_dimension: 5
            writer_extensions:
            {
                HasVerilogMemset: {}
            }
            // writer_junctions: the 2->1 operator class at the DATA SWITCH (not in an extension chain). A junction
            // consumes the arriving remote partial AND this node's local operand and emits one stream, which is what
            // enables the CHAINGATHER / GATHERROOT switch modes -- reduce hop-by-hop along the route instead of
            // gathering everything at a root. The first two are built so the linear and the nonlinear case sit on ONE
            // framework and can be compared like-for-like:
            //   ElementwiseJunction -- the LINEAR baseline: a 2-input per-element FP reduction (ADD/MUL/MAX/MIN),
            //     i.e. exactly the operator a collective-capable NoC puts inside the router. Runtime FP16/BF16/FP32,
            //     plus a native-width integer grid (INT8/16/32).
            //   MonoidJunction     -- the NONLINEAR family the per-element form cannot express at all: the online-
            //     softmax (m, l) merge, the flash-attention (m, l, O) triple, exp-weighted moments, argmax. One
            //     netlist, selected by the geometry fields of its CSR word.
            // Both are stateless in the operand pair, so the fold is fully pipelined (no accBusy read-modify-write)
            // and the join is cut-through: first-output latency does not grow with payload (measured 9 CC / 7 CC,
            // util 1.000), which is what keeps a reduce-along-the-route chain latency-competitive with a star.
            //
            // OPERATORS ON ONE SOCKET. The host takes a LIST, allocates each entry its own user CSRs and arms
            // exactly one per transfer via the enable bitmask -- so an operator is a plug-in, not a mode.
            // Editing this list regenerates XDMA_DST_JCT_* and the WRITER_JCT_* defines, so SW must be rebuilt.
            writer_junctions:
            {
                HasElementwiseJunction: {dataWidth: 512, elemWidth: 16, fpPipe: 1}
                HasMonoidJunction: {dataWidth: 512, fpPipe: 1, expLutN: 128}
                // TopKJunction: an operator from OUTSIDE the classified monoid family -- its own beat layout,
                // no key front end, no exponential and no FMA -- on the same socket, satisfying the same four
                // obligations. It is the evidence that the CONTRACT composes, not the monoid cell.
                HasTopKJunction: {dataWidth: 512, k: 8}
                // the operator with no arithmetic: OR / AND / XOR over the raw beat
                HasBitwiseJunction: {dataWidth: 512}
            }
            reader_extensions: {
                HasTransposer: {row:[8,8], col:[8,8], elementWidth:[8,16]}
                HasElementwiseAdd: {elementWidth: 32, dataWidth: 512}
                // computeLanes time-mux the per-lane FP units for area; fpPipe = internal FP-unit pipeline
                // depth (the per-op "cutting" knob to meet timing), range 0..2 (0 = combinational FP ops).
                // StreamReduce also has treePipe: a SEPARATE 0..2 cut depth for the horizontal reduce-tree adds.
                // These are also what computes each cluster's LOCAL flash-attention partial (m_i, l_i) before a
                // ChainGather merges them: StreamReduce (MAX, SUM), StreamMap (EXP), StreamElementwise (-max).
                HasStreamMap: {dataWidth: 512, elementWidth: 16, computeLanes: 4, func: ["LINEAR_FP16", "EXP_FP16", "SILU_FP16"], fpPipe: 1}
                // op-set = the single fused FMA op (add/square accumulate, op CSR selects) + the MAX compare.
                HasStreamReduce: {dataWidth: 512, elementWidth: 16, computeLanes: 4, op: ["FMA_FP16", "MAX_FP16"], fpPipe: 1, treePipe: 1, treeLanes: 2}
                // op-set = the single fused FMA op (MUL = acc*x, ADD = acc+x; op CSR selects).
                HasStreamElementwise: {dataWidth: 512, elementWidth: 16, computeLanes: 4, op: ["FMA_FP16"], fpPipe: 1}
                HasFp16ToInt8: {in_elementWidth: 16, out_elementWidth: 8, dataWidth: 512, computeLanes: 4, fpPipe: 1}
            }
        }
        // Xdiv_sqrt: true,
        # isa: "rv32ema",
        xdma: true
        xssr: false
        xfrep: false
        xf16: false,
        xf16alt: false,
        xf8: false,
        xf8alt: false,
        xfdotp: false,
        xfvec: false,
        num_int_outstanding_loads: 1,
        num_int_outstanding_mem: 4,
        num_fp_outstanding_loads: 4,
        num_fp_outstanding_mem: 4,
        num_sequencer_instructions: 16,
        num_dtlb_entries: 1,
        num_itlb_entries: 1,
    },
    // SNAX Streamer Templates
    snax_streamer_gemmX_streamer_template :{

        data_reader_params: {
            spatial_bounds: [[8], [8]],
            temporal_dim: [6, 3],
            num_channel: [8, 8],
            fifo_depth: [8, 8],
            configurable_channel: [0, 0],
            tcdm_logic_word_size: [[256, 128, 64], [256, 128, 64]],
            datapath_extensions: [{HasTransposer: {row:[8], col:[8], elementWidth:[8]}}, {HasTransposer: {row:[8], col:[8], elementWidth:[8]}}]
        },

        data_writer_params:{
            spatial_bounds: [[8]],
            temporal_dim: [3],
            num_channel: [8],
            fifo_depth: [1],
            configurable_channel: [0],
            tcdm_logic_word_size: [[256, 128, 64]],
        },

        data_reader_writer_params:{
            spatial_bounds: [[8, 4], [8, 4]],
            temporal_dim: [3, 3],
            num_channel: [32, 32],
            fifo_depth: [1, 1],
            configurable_channel: [1, 0],
            tcdm_logic_word_size: [[256, 128, 64], [256, 128, 64]],
            datapath_extensions: [{HasBroadcaster: {inputLength: 256, outputLength: 2048}}, {}]
        },

        # needs to be ketp for csr num calculation in snax_gen.py
        has_transpose: true,

        has_C_broadcast: true,

        snax_library_name: "gemmx",
    }
}